<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="150" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H12a: YamlDotNet manifest engine + DV-REST seed writes</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-5 -- Seed</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Replaces a shell-out to a script requiring a second PowerShell module (powershell-yaml) -- a DS-1b matrix-correction item; feeds the AI seed chain (ADR-039 playbook consumers).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified port reusing an EXISTING in-process idiom (H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter) -- Sonnet @ high per DS-1b's 4-5 person-day estimate.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>waveG5-parallel</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>141</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, option-d, sdk-port, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Port H12aAiSeedChainHandler.cs's collaborator InvokeSeedManifestScriptRunner (seed-data/Invoke-SeedManifest.ps1, 536 lines: Install-Module powershell-yaml + Dataverse Web API Invoke-RestMethod under ambient az token) to YamlDotNet (manifest parse) + Dataverse Web API HttpClient writes -- THE EXACT PATTERN H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter ALREADY USES IN-PROCESS (reuse that idiom, do not invent a new one). Seed manifests become embedded content files in the payload (needed under every architecture option, not merely Option D). This CLOSES the DS-1b matrix-correction finding: 'DS-1 §1.2 exactly one PowerShell module is wrong -- Invoke-SeedManifest.ps1:162-165 requires powershell-yaml (a second module)' -- YamlDotNet eliminates that second-module dependency entirely.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in YamlDotNet manifest parsing and the Dataverse Web API upsert idiom H12c already proves in-process.</role>

  <goal>H12aAiSeedChainHandler.cs's manifest-driven seed collaborator is a pure .NET implementation: YamlDotNet parses the seed manifest (now an embedded content file, not a filesystem path), and Dataverse Web API HttpClient writes perform the seed upserts, following the SAME in-process pattern H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter already ships. manifest-hash idempotency (re-running an unchanged manifest is a no-op) and per-step outcome classification are preserved from the script's existing semantics.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b §1 (H12a row, collaborator #22) explicitly names the reuse target: 'YamlDotNet (manifest parse) + Dataverse Web API HttpClient (the EXACT pattern H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter already uses in-process); seed manifests become content files in the payload (needed under every option).' DS-1b §1's 'Matrix corrections to DS-1's fact base' section flags the powershell-yaml second-module finding this task's YamlDotNet port directly resolves.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/H12aAiSeedChainHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/YamlSeedManifestEngine.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/DataverseWebApiSeedWriter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/seed-data/Invoke-SeedManifest.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/RuntimeReferences/H12cRuntimeReferencesHandler.cs (the in-process idiom to reuse)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="141" status="pending">H6 must have imported the solutions/tables H12a seeds into</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-1b §1 H12a row">REUSE H12c's exact in-process Dataverse Web API upsert idiom -- do not invent a second, parallel Dataverse-write helper for H12a when one already exists and is proven.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md">H12a seeds playbook consumers per ADR-039's single-AI-routing-surface model -- verify the seed manifest's playbook-consumer entries match the ADR-039 shape (spaarke-playbook-embeddings retired).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H12a YamlDotNet manifest engine port</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="In-process Dataverse Web API upsert (reuse)" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/RuntimeReferences/">H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter already proves the exact HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential upsert pattern H12a's seed writer reuses.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read Invoke-SeedManifest.ps1 in full plus H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter in full as the reuse target.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Manifest as content">Move the seed manifest(s) into embedded content files consumed at runtime (not a filesystem path).</step>
    <step order="2" name="YamlSeedManifestEngine">Author the YamlDotNet-based parser producing the same in-memory manifest shape the script's downstream logic consumed.</step>
    <step order="3" name="DataverseWebApiSeedWriter">Author the writer reusing H12c's exact upsert idiom for the seed rows this manifest declares.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Idempotency">Preserve manifest-hash idempotency semantics (re-run of an unchanged manifest = no-op) per the script's existing behavior.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire up">Replace InvokeSeedManifestScriptRunner in H12a's owning module with the new implementation.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Tests">manifest-hash idempotency tests + per-step outcome tests per DS-4 §7's test-effort note.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'powershell-yaml\|ProcessStartInfo' in the new files returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the seed manifest's YAML shape uses a feature YamlDotNet's default deserializer does not support out-of-the-box (a custom PowerShell-yaml-specific extension), STOP and escalate to determine whether the manifest itself should be simplified or a custom YamlDotNet type converter is warranted — do not silently drop unsupported manifest fields.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/YamlSeedManifestEngine.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/DataverseWebApiSeedWriter.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'powershell-yaml\|Install-Module\|ProcessStartInfo' in the new H12a collaborator files returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms re-running the seed process against an UNCHANGED manifest is a no-op (manifest-hash idempotency).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms the writer reuses H12c's upsert idiom (same request-shape pattern, verified by comparing the constructed HTTP requests' shape) rather than a parallel implementation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H12c's RuntimeReferencesWriter already proves the exact in-process Dataverse upsert pattern this task's writer reuses; nothing new to invent there. Extension -- adding YamlDotNet as the manifest-parse layer (replacing a second PowerShell module dependency) while reusing the proven writer idiom is the minimal correct move. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H12a cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site; separately, the powershell-yaml second-module dependency (a DS-1b matrix-correction finding) would otherwise persist as an unnecessary Option-D image-spec gap even under a fat-container fallback.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
